      "level": "5",
      "school": "Necromancy",
      "caster": "priest",
      "verbal": true,
      "somatic": true,
      "material": true,
      "materials": "",
      "range": "120 yards",
      "aoe": "1 creature per level",
      "casting_time": "8",
      "duration": "Permanent",
      "save": "Neg.",
      "damage": "",
      "description": "Victims of this spell are afflicted with a **horrific magical disease** if they fail a **save vs. spell at –3**:\n\n- Covered in **boils, lesions, cysts**\n- **Strength, Dexterity, and Charisma –3**\n- **Attack rolls –3**\n\nCured only by *cure disease*, *heal*, or *restoration* from a **more powerful priest** than the caster. **Dispel magic** and *remove curse* do **not** work; *wish* will cure it instantly.\n\nNeglected scourges can lead to **long-term illness** and **death within 1–4 weeks**. In populated areas, a **1% chance per caster level** exists of **triggering an epidemic**.\n\n**Material component**: A specially prepared **black whip or crop**, cracked at the target during casting【139:3†TSR 2151 - The Complete Book of Necromancers.pdf】.",
